          "physical_page": 1,
          "text": "2026 Development Impact Fee Schedule \n",
          "native_start": 598,
          "native_end": 636,
          "candidate_native_offset": 56,
          "candidate_start": 654,
          "candidate_end": 692,
          "candidate_path": "/private/tmp/geode-clean-archive-2f2b450/research/local_review/ebenezer-016-017-reconciliation-2026-09-12/historical-packet/baseline/EB-PDF-016/inputs/candidate.txt",
          "sha256": "c406d7eeba71995b55212c5ed6280bedf3c4af927937a9f68eeb8d15f221a9d7"
        }
      ],
      "page_image_paths": [
        "/private/tmp/geode-clean-archive-2f2b450/research/local_review/ebenezer-016-017-reconciliation-2026-09-12/historical-packet/baseline/EB-PDF-016/inputs/page-0001.png"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p1-chunk-4",
      "role": "body",
      "statement": "Unchanged source span",
      "qualification": "visible",
      "native_spans": [
        {
          "physical_page": 1,
          "text": "FINANCE DEPARTMENT \nMEMORANDUM \nDATE: \nNovember 1, 2025 \nFROM: \nCity of Greeley, Colorado \nRE: \n2026 Development Impact Fees \nIn the 2023 adoption of the Police, Fire, Park, Trails, Storm Drainage, and Transportation development \nimpact fees, the methodology to adjust fees annually was adopted. City of Greeley Code Chapter \n4.64.055(b) states that the fees will be recalculated by applying the Economic Adjustment Factor \n(EAF). \nThe EAF is determined on an annual basis, using six weighted data variables, considered to be \nrepresentative of economic growth, the cost of materials and services associated with constructing \ncapital projects, and general economic conditions. The variables include: \n Percent change in Greeley Utility Customer Accounts – representing the growth and scope of \npublic services; \n Percent change in CDOT Construction Cost Index – representing the cost of providing \ntransportation networks; \n Percent change in Engineering News Records Construction Cost Index – representing material \ncosts associated with capital projects; \n Percent change in Engineering News Records Building Cost Index – representing labor costs \nassociated with capital projects; \n Percent change in Assessed Value of Greeley Real Property – representing growth and the \neconomic value of real property assets; and \n Percent change in Greeley MSA Employment – representing a general indicator of the \neconomic health of the area. \nThe 2026 EAF was calculated using the most reliable and consistent annual data sets from the \nprevious full year. Since the EAF is calculated on November 1, 2025, for the 2026 fee year, the \npercent change was calculated using year end 2024 compared to year end 2023. \n",
          "native_start": 636,
          "native_end": 2371,
          "candidate_native_offset": 56,
          "candidate_start": 692,
          "candidate_end": 2427,
          "candidate_path": "/private/tmp/geode-clean-archive-2f2b450/research/local_review/ebenezer-016-017-reconciliation-2026-09-12/historical-packet/baseline/EB-PDF-016/inputs/candidate.txt",
          "sha256": "5ba28cec807067b0352aa1672420b37bf2477645a465c87d13a7f5486f737001"
        }
      ],
      "page_image_paths": [
        "/private/tmp/geode-clean-archive-2f2b450/research/local_review/ebenezer-016-017-reconciliation-2026-09-12/historical-packet/baseline/EB-PDF-016/inputs/page-0001.png"
      ]
